** Make sure to run configuration prior to the first Carbyne Stack CLI command execution ** 
 
 This command will guide through a step by step configuration to match the VC's setup. 
 While it is required to run the configuration at least once prior to the first command execution, it is possible to overload some settings using environment variables. 
 The following environment variables can be used to adapt the configuration without overwriting the default config. 
 - CS_PRIME 	 Modulus N as used by the MPC backend - CS_R 	 Auxiliary modulus R as used by the MPC backend - CS_R_INV 	 Multiplicative inverse for the auxiliary modulus R as used by the MPC backend 
 - CS_NO_SSL_VALIDATION 	 Disable SSL certificate validation 
 - CS_VCP_{n}_BASE_URL** 	 Base URL for the provider with ID "{n}" - CS_VCP_{n}_AMPHORA_URL* 	 Amphora Service URL for the provider with ID "{n}" 
 - CS_VCP_{n}_CASTOR_URL* 	 Castor Service URL for the provider with ID "{n}" 
 - CS_VCP_{n}_EPHEMERAL_URL* 	 Ephemeral Service URL for the provider with ID "{n}" 
 - CS_VCP_{n}_OAUTH2_CLIENT_ID * 	 OAuth2 client identifier for the provider with ID "{n}" 
 - CS_VCP_{n}_OAUTH2_CALLBACK_URL * 	 OAuth2 callback URL for the provider with ID "{n}" 
 - CS_VCP_{n}_OAUTH2_AUTH_ENDPOINT_URI * 	 OAuth2 authorization endpoint URI for the provider with ID "{n}" 
 - CS_VCP_{n}_OAUTH2_TOKEN_ENDPOINT_URI * 	 OAuth2 token endpoint URI for the provider with ID "{n}" 
 
 * Please be aware, that only providers defined in the default configuration can be adapted using environment variables. It is not possible to add additional or remove existing providers. 
 ** This variable is used during the configuration process only.
